+We make four contributions. (1) The APIP, a formalized post-deployment
+remediation lifecycle protocol grounded in organizational management and
+training evaluation research. (2) A five-category failure-mode taxonomy, with
+a published deterministic mapping from trace-level annotations (MAST
+\cite{cemri2025}) and disaggregation signatures onto taxonomy categories and
+intervention tiers. (3) A three-tier intervention hierarchy with escalation
+criteria, evaluated through Kirkpatrick's framework, and a declarative APIP
+schema for tooling and audit trails. (4) An end-to-end evaluation of the
+protocol in two live multi-agent environments against no-action, always-
+Tier-1, and oracle baselines, with an attribution accounting scored against
+injected ground truth; a null result also suggests that mesh disruption
+requires a bounded shared context.
 
